      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Application Read-only Queries",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Application Read-only Queries",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "5pLYEFBUiRBYR4p3TDA64",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 93.12678936225188,
      "y": 1526.3828619661779,
      "width": 1191.76513671875,
      "height": 1000.0000000000003,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1Q",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1723148372,
      "version": 482,
      "versionNonce": 1016001772,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "s8yywatHl7Mpk3OYRHTo-",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1788463343877,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "System Architecture & Features (Diagram Highlights)\n\n* **Bounded Load Shedding (Backpressure Protection)**\n* Restricts queue size to prevent out-of-memory (OOM) kernel panics.\n\n\n* Instantly returns `[ERROR] SERVER_BUSY_QUEUE_FULL` and closes sockets when max capacity is reached.\n\n\n\n\n* **Request Coalescing / Leader Election (Thundering Herd Defense)**\n* Avoids duplicate database fetches when multiple concurrent clients miss the exact same key simultaneously.\n\n\n* The first thread becomes the Leader to fetch data from PostgreSQL; all following threads block on the node-level condition variable until signaled.\n\n\n\n\n* **Passive Lazy TTL Invalidation**\n* Eliminates background polling threads that cause cache-wide lock contention.\n\n\n* Invalidation checks occur on-demand during lookup: expired items are removed and immediately re-routed to the Leader-election fetch path.\n\n\n\n\n* **Fixed Server Pool vs. Dynamic Client Load**\n* Server worker count remains fixed at boot to match database connection pool constraints.\n\n\n* Handles dynamic client-side load scaling smoothly by buffering surplus work in the task queue.\n\n\n\n\n* **Zero TCP Handshake Overhead for Database Reads**\n* Uses a dedicated connection pool to eliminate the cost of renegotiating PostgreSQL authentication and TCP handshakes per query.\n\n\n\n\n* **Real-Time Telemetry Dashboard**\n* Streams live metrics over TCP using dedicated commands (`STATS`, `STATS_JSON`) without disrupting query execution threads.\n\n\n* Integrates with a lightweight web interface to visualize live throughput, hit rates, active threads, and comparative DB latency.",
      "fontSize": 16.326530612244902,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "System Architecture & Features (Diagram Highlights)\n\n* **Bounded Load Shedding (Backpressure Protection)**\n* Restricts queue size to prevent out-of-memory (OOM) kernel panics.\n\n\n* Instantly returns `[ERROR] SERVER_BUSY_QUEUE_FULL` and closes sockets when max capacity is reached.\n\n\n\n\n* **Request Coalescing / Leader Election (Thundering Herd Defense)**\n* Avoids duplicate database fetches when multiple concurrent clients miss the exact same key simultaneously.\n\n\n* The first thread becomes the Leader to fetch data from PostgreSQL; all following threads block on the node-level condition variable until signaled.\n\n\n\n\n* **Passive Lazy TTL Invalidation**\n* Eliminates background polling threads that cause cache-wide lock contention.\n\n\n* Invalidation checks occur on-demand during lookup: expired items are removed and immediately re-routed to the Leader-election fetch path.\n\n\n\n\n* **Fixed Server Pool vs. Dynamic Client Load**\n* Server worker count remains fixed at boot to match database connection pool constraints.\n\n\n* Handles dynamic client-side load scaling smoothly by buffering surplus work in the task queue.\n\n\n\n\n* **Zero TCP Handshake Overhead for Database Reads**\n* Uses a dedicated connection pool to eliminate the cost of renegotiating PostgreSQL authentication and TCP handshakes per query.\n\n\n\n\n* **Real-Time Telemetry Dashboard**\n* Streams live metrics over TCP using dedicated commands (`STATS`, `STATS_JSON`) without disrupting query execution threads.\n\n\n* Integrates with a lightweight web interface to visualize live throughput, hit rates, active threads, and comparative DB latency.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "i-ANGKEJfvRjl6maURsYq",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1051.6865572929385,
      "y": 887.6755762894949,
      "width": 564.1550940088495,
      "height": 256.25000000000034,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1R",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 511074540,
      "version": 323,
      "versionNonce": 1521827540,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788462589725,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "DETAILS\n\n* std::unordered_map<std::string,\nstd::list<std::shared_ptr<CacheNode>>::iterator>\n(Directory)\n* Provides strict O(1) key lookup for incoming SQL\nqueries.\n* Maps each query directly to a node's iterator\ninside the doubly-linked list for instant access\nwithout traversal.",
      "fontSize": 20.50000000000003,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "DETAILS\n\n* std::unordered_map<std::string, std::list<std::shared_ptr<CacheNode>>::iterator> (Directory)\n* Provides strict O(1) key lookup for incoming SQL queries.\n* Maps each query directly to a node's iterator inside the doubly-linked list for instant access without traversal.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
