    {
      "id": "loPumg_Pc9Cf-7JAaOweN",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1882.2971568788803,
      "y": 1458.1664195174126,
      "width": 798.3671875,
      "height": 1050,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 2,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2G",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1514944748,
      "version": 8,
      "versionNonce": 215787604,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788462218197,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "System Architecture & Features (Diagram Highlights)\n\n- Bounded Load Shedding (Backpressure Protection)\nRestricts queue size to prevent out-of-memory (OOM)\nkernel panics.  Instantly returns [ERROR]\nSERVER_BUSY_QUEUE_FULL and closes sockets when\nmax capacity is reached.  Request Coalescing / Leader\nElection (Thundering Herd Defense)Avoids duplicate\ndatabase fetches when multiple concurrent clients miss\nthe exact same key simultaneously.  The first thread\nbecomes the Leader to fetch data from PostgreSQL; all\nfollowing threads block on the node-level condition\nvariable until signaled.  Passive Lazy TTL\nInvalidationEliminates background polling threads that\ncause cache-wide lock contention.  Invalidation checks\noccur on-demand during lookup: expired items are removed\nand immediately re-routed to the Leader-election fetch\npath.  Fixed Server Pool vs. Dynamic Client LoadServer\nworker count remains fixed at boot to match database\nconnection pool constraints.  Handles dynamic client-side\nload scaling smoothly by buffering surplus work in the\ntask queue.  Zero TCP Handshake Overhead for\nDatabase ReadsUses a dedicated connection pool to\neliminate the cost of renegotiating PostgreSQL\nauthentication and TCP handshakes per query.  Real-Time\nTelemetry DashboardStreams live metrics over TCP using\ndedicated commands (STATS, STATS_JSON) without\ndisrupting query execution threads.  Integrates with a\nlightweight web interface to visualize live throughput, hit\nrates, active threads, and comparative DB latency.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "System Architecture & Features (Diagram Highlights)\n\n- Bounded Load Shedding (Backpressure Protection)\nRestricts queue size to prevent out-of-memory (OOM) kernel panics.  Instantly returns [ERROR] SERVER_BUSY_QUEUE_FULL and closes sockets when max capacity is reached.  Request Coalescing / Leader Election (Thundering Herd Defense)Avoids duplicate database fetches when multiple concurrent clients miss the exact same key simultaneously.  The first thread becomes the Leader to fetch data from PostgreSQL; all following threads block on the node-level condition variable until signaled.  Passive Lazy TTL InvalidationEliminates background polling threads that cause cache-wide lock contention.  Invalidation checks occur on-demand during lookup: expired items are removed and immediately re-routed to the Leader-election fetch path.  Fixed Server Pool vs. Dynamic Client LoadServer worker count remains fixed at boot to match database connection pool constraints.  Handles dynamic client-side load scaling smoothly by buffering surplus work in the task queue.  Zero TCP Handshake Overhead for Database ReadsUses a dedicated connection pool to eliminate the cost of renegotiating PostgreSQL authentication and TCP handshakes per query.  Real-Time Telemetry DashboardStreams live metrics over TCP using dedicated commands (STATS, STATS_JSON) without disrupting query execution threads.  Integrates with a lightweight web interface to visualize live throughput, hit rates, active threads, and comparative DB latency.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "TNxHdaAP2e9VY0TTCvKv6",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1209.2063728854778,
      "y": 1357.5073324157954,
      "width": 595.5672936817966,
      "height": 362.50000000000074,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 2,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2H",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1819939564,
      "version": 341,
      "versionNonce": 398773356,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "AmbRV8R-18117Mt32jIMe",
          "type": "arrow"
        },
        {
          "id": "V8c8x1iDz_-yV5Y9gWaHq",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1788462721320,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "FEATURES\n\n* Request Coalescing / Leader Election (Thundering Herd\nDefense) - Avoids duplicate database fetches when\nmultiple concurrent clients miss the exact same key\nsimultaneously.\n* The first thread becomes the Leader to fetch data from\nDataBase; all following threads block on the node-level\ncondition variable until signaled.\n\n* Passive Lazy TTL Invalidation - Eliminates background\npolling threads that cause cache-wide lock contention.\n* Invalidation checks occur on-demand during lookup:\nexpired items are removed and immediately re-routed to\nthe Leader-election fetch path.",
      "fontSize": 19.333333333333375,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "FEATURES\n\n* Request Coalescing / Leader Election (Thundering Herd Defense) - Avoids duplicate database fetches when multiple concurrent clients miss the exact same key simultaneously.\n* The first thread becomes the Leader to fetch data from DataBase; all following threads block on the node-level condition variable until signaled.\n\n* Passive Lazy TTL Invalidation - Eliminates background polling threads that cause cache-wide lock contention.\n* Invalidation checks occur on-demand during lookup: expired items are removed and immediately re-routed to the Leader-election fetch path.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
